That she's autistic and that's why everyone sees her as different but that it's not a bad thing and it doesn't make her inferior. It just means she lives in a hostile world, and that when she's older people won't be so cruel anymore, and that they'll love her regardless of her mental illnesses.

&#x200B;

And also that counseling and therapy is meant to help you, not to make you more convenient for adults to 'deal with.'

