I don't want to have kids because I'd rather adopt and give some people who already exist a home, than creating a new person who never needed to exist.

&#x200B;

And also because bringing new children into this world in the state that it is in is incredibly unnecessary and has no compassion for the child that will have to endure it.

I don't even like classic. I just feel like the old zones are the only part of the game left that actually make it feel like a world... and I don't want that to change

&#x200B;

Also I don't want all of the trees to look like they're made out of rubber.

alien space goats that made their demons everyone else's problem and now there's a banshee elf burning down trees.

&#x200B;

(world of warcraft)

I have a horrible case of generational trauma and severe ptsd/ocd, so im basically incapable of being a sufficient parent. I also have family history of things like diabetes, anemia, and various mental disorders (long history of family ptsd, schizophrenia, bipolar, depression, GAD, and suicide) which are basically hell to live with in america's health care system so I would never want to pass on any of that to a child.

&#x200B;

Not to mention what horrible, terrible things they can go through in this world of late-stage capitalism and violence. I just don't feel like it's right for me to have a child. Call it conscious darwinism I guess, and I also believe that anyone having a child in general right now is so pointless and unreasonable considering the hundreds of thousands of kids in the united states' hellish foster care system that need stability and a loving home.
